      "notes": "DeKalb County (pop. 764,000; Atlanta metro east and north core) should not be confused with DeKalb County IL (FIPS 17037) or DeKalb County IN in the atlas. The GA DeKalb parcel REST layer at dcgis.dekalbcountyga.gov/hosted/rest/services/Parcels/MapServer exposes 20+ confirmed fields. PARCELID is an 11-digit identifier with spaces (e.g., '06 249 03 007') reflecting district, map sheet, block, and parcel components. Owner fields: OWNERNME1/2. Site address: SITEADDRESS. The CVTTXCD and CVTTXDSCRP fields identify the city/tax district, which matters because several cities -- Decatur, Brookhaven, Dunwoody, Tucker, Doraville, Stone Mountain -- maintain separate municipal boundaries within the county. SCHLTXCD and SCHLDSCRP identify the school tax district. Classification: USECD, USEDSCRP, CLASSCD, CLASSDSCRP, and PRPRTYDSCRP. Verified 2026-05-15: SMITH returns Doraville and Atlanta-DeKalb addresses. For full assessment and exemption records, the DeKalb County Tax Commissioner portal at tax.dekalbcountyga.gov is the authoritative lookup."
